{"id": "EUVD-2026-108867", "enisaUuid": "196c68c8-486a-3e03-a483-62e2d1a86c76", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndpaa2-switch: fix the error path in dpaa2_switch_rx()\n\nIn case of an error in dpaa2_switch_rx(), the dpaa2_switch_free_fd()\nfunction is called in order to free the FD. This is incorrect since the\ndpaa2_switch_free_fd() is intended to be used on Tx frame descriptors,\nmeaning that it expects in the software annotation area of the FD data\nto find a valid skb pointer on which to call dev_kfree_skb().\n\nFix this by extracting the dma_unmap_page() from\ndpaa2_switch_build_linear_skb() directly into the dpaa2_switch_rx()\nfunction. This allows us to directly use free_pages() in case of an\nerror before an SKB was created and kfree_skb() afterwards.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:38", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/791068c962469af0090e1a1ee63657fb9eef40db", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee54f8d7e642c44cfcc2dcb390b4c50e145d81b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/259ad6093204b999d41e7e6d0ad90ef9a71a44ab", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f4ceb8e3d6d5becb4cda7a7098a8638e18c835a1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fa232b4496cb59503ae5108c756cbe10e59b0bc3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/74c1c9f5c0c30bbd0c2cf87b6e3507e7ea46c13d", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98911"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98911", "GHSA-2gxg-jvpv-v5rf"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07c353da-d032-32a8-b1c8-757da7da6369", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "0912300c-3b7b-3acc-a191-46b79a7ed0e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <791068c962469af0090e1a1ee63657fb9eef40db"}, {"id": "0e504b78-725a-3c19-ab29-51fe7a443c20", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "